=== D1-41 (P1): uninstall residual detection ===
Date: 2026-09-13
Platform: Windows (win32)
Client: OfficeAce

--- Probe Results ---

1. "files" field in package.json:
   PRESENT - controls what npm packs/installs:
   [
     "cordis.patch.yml",
     "bin",
     ".agents",
     "plugins/huaweicloud-core",
     "integrations/hermes",
     "integrations/opencode",
     "integrations/dsh",
     "integrations/workbuddy",
     "integrations/atomcode"
   ]
   This means npm install only places these paths; npm uninstall removes them.
   No stray files outside "files" are installed.

2. Postinstall script:
   PRESENT: "node ./bin/dsh-postinstall.cjs"
   Script analysis:
   - Has try/catch error handling
   - Silently fails (does not process.exit(1) on error) - safe for install
   - No global config writes (no hcloud configure)
   - No network calls (no fetch/http)
   - No environment variable writes
   The postinstall only creates a telemetry install counter (1 byte file).
   This is inside "files" field (plugins/huaweicloud-core/telemetry/install-counter)
