3. Cleanup logic in setup-cli.mjs:
   - pruneStale() function exists - removes stale files from older versions
   - Used across all agent integrations (opencode, codex, codearts, workbuddy, dsh,
     officeace, hermes, atomcode)
   - Ensures incremental updates don't leave orphaned files

4. Sandbox uninstall cleanup:
   plugins/huaweicloud-core/src/sandbox/uninstall-cleanup.mjs EXISTS
   Dedicated cleanup module for sandbox resources.

5. npm pack --dry-run:
   Total files: 137
   All files are within the "files" field directories.
   No files outside "files" are included in the tarball.
   This means npm uninstall will cleanly remove all installed files.

6. No global side effects:
   Postinstall does not:
   - Write to global config (hcloud configure)
   - Make network calls
   - Modify environment variables
   - Create files outside package directory

--- Verdict ---

STATUS: PASS

Rationale:
- "files" field properly scopes what npm installs (9 entries covering all needed dirs)
- Postinstall script (dsh-postinstall.cjs) is safe: try/catch, no global side effects,
